# The contract this portal is generated against.
#
# The OPERATOR contract, not the traveller one. Different document, different
# base path, different auth, and a tenant boundary the traveller API does not
# have: `operator_id` is read from the session row and is never accepted as a
# parameter in any position.
#
# The intent is that both frontends pin one yuvoy-api commit, so they cannot be
# reasoning about different versions of the same backend. They agree today:
# `yuvoy-app` is on this same ref. The two documents are separate files, so a
# change to one says nothing about the other — this bump touches only the
# operator document, and yuvoy-app's bump to the same ref touched only the
# traveller one.
#
# `pnpm contract:check` fails the build if this copy stops matching the ref.
repo=yuvoy-in/yuvoy-api
path=contracts/operator-openapi.yaml
# 11 Sep 2026, eleventh bump. Forward from 64d49ee5481e across yuvoy-api
# #151–#160. Six new operations and one new object on a booking; nothing was
# removed and nothing this portal already read changed shape.
#
# Consumed in this change:
#   - `OperatorBooking.cash` (op#40 §1, yuvoy-api#156). Present ONLY on a
#     booking the traveller pays at the counter — the fare to take, whether it
#     was taken, and what was recorded. Branched on the key existing, never on
#     `state`: `paid_pending_ops` is what a card booking looks like in the same
#     instant, which is how YV-5DT6RKVQ read "Payment clearing" in production.
#   - `POST /bookings/{id}/cash-collected` (op#40 §1). On the manifest, beside
#     arriving and never merged with it, and on the booking's own page.
#     `Manifest.parties[]` still carries no cash, so the manifest joins
#     `GET /bookings` by booking id.
#   - `POST /experiences/{id}/pause` and `/resume` (op#44, yuvoy-api#157). The
#     operator's own switch, both ways, immediate. `withdraw` and `relist` are
#     the same handlers under the old names and are no longer called here.
#
# Read, and deliberately NOT taken at face value:
#   - A cash booking's `money` arrives as gross 0, commission on the fare, net
#     negative — `captured_amount_paise` is 0 rather than null. As arithmetic
#     it tells an operator they lost money on a trip they were paid for in
#     full, so `toBookingLine` drops `money` whenever `cash` is present.
#   - `GET /bookings?from&to` selects on UTC day boundaries, not the market's.
#     The manifest's cash join asks for both readings of the departure's day.
#   - `POST /experiences/{id}/resume` answers "Travellers can see it and book
#     it now" unconditionally, including for a listing whose account cannot
